The Android tile, over t715-android

Waydroid's own tile, after the SD card one: on while the Android session is
running ("Asleep" while the container is frozen), off when it is stopped. A tap
starts or stops the session in the background (t715-android start / stop) and
probes again 5 s later; a long press opens Android's Settings app (t715-android
settings). Without the command or when Waydroid is not installed no android key
is probed and the tile stays dimmed, so an image without t715-android or a
kernel without binder never fails. Ported from the SM-T715's 0.2.94 series
(image/pkg/omamobile-shell/0013-tablet-android-tile.patch of the owner's
repository); against omamobile 899184543d60 (omamobile-shell 0.2.147) and the
patches before it (0001-0015), packages/omamobile-shell.

